regex captures all three entries by running it against the file.

## Errors & Mistakes
First placement of the renovate-release marker left comment paragraphs between
it and the pin line; the custom manager's matchString requires the digest line
IMMEDIATELY after the marker, so the K3 entry silently did not match. Caught
by executing the regex from renovate.json5 against the file before committing.

## Dead Ends
github-tags as a middle ground: no tag exists on the branch and renovate
cannot express "first tag containing this commit".

## Hints for Future Agents
Always verify marker placement by running the matchStrings regex from
.github/renovate.json5 against the config file; adjacency is load-bearing.
versioning=loose is fine for git-refs digest bumps (only currentDigest moves).
Expect red renovate PRs when upstream bumps the FlashInfer floor — that is the
designed signal that flashinfer-patches/v0.6.15.post1/ needs re-keying.

## Codebase Discoveries
The custom manager captures depName verbatim as the package name, so git-refs
entries need the full https URL as depName.

